## Store Family (canonical registries)

Each of these owns one kind of record and hands out the id everything else joins on. Four are named in `~/AGENTS.md` as the backend an agent **must** use for a given job, so an agent can be sent to one of these without this file ever mentioning it — that was true for months and is what this section fixes. `model-store`, `agent-store` and `tool-store` are the same family and are listed under Core Agent System; `harness-store`, `memory-store`, `hook-store`, `snapshot-store` and `repo-store`'s `repodetect` sit under the LLM Bridge tables.

| Project | Type | Language | Description |
|---------|------|----------|-------------|
| **auth-store** | Service | Go | `:8303`. The credential vault: OAuth provider plugins, interactive login, server-side refresh of stored tokens, audit log. dash resolves its Google Calendar token from here. Replaces `apiauth`. **`~/AGENTS.md` orders every agent to use it for credentials, API keys and OAuth.** |
| **skill-store** | Service | Go | `:8301`. Registry of Claude Code / Agent `SKILL.md` skills, ingested by cloning an upstream repo — or, since 2026-08-04, by reading a directory on this host — and walking it for `SKILL.md`. Data in `~/.config/skill-store/`. **The Directives section above tells every agent to query it before any non-trivial task.** |
| **kanban-store** | Service | Go | `:8305`. Board and card *placement*, treating **noteboard as the source of truth for card content** — it stores where a card sits, not what it says. Publishes an entity-type registry so agents can resolve entity refs themselves; deliberately dumb, it does not proxy to those services. |
| **event-store** | Service | Go | `:8308`. Backend for the personal events radar: `sources` (where to look — `watch`, `research` or `scout`, each with its own cadence and effort tier) and the candidate `events` they yield, approved onto Google Calendar from the Suggestions panel. **See the events rules in `~/AGENTS.md`: send `"status":"proposed"` on every source you add, and never self-approve.** |
| **job-store** | Service | Go | `:8311`. The job radar, and deliberately the same shape as event-store: `sources` (where to look — `board`, `research` or `scout`, each with its own `cadence_hours`), the `listings` they yield, the `documents` you apply with (resume and cover-letter variants, plus tailoring requests) and the `applications` made from them. Six canonical role families served by `GET /role-families`, so no UI builds a filter from observed values. **Everything a scout finds arrives `proposed`; nothing self-approves** — `PATCH /sources/{id}` is the decision channel. Routes are rooted at `/`, not `/api` (`GET /listings`, `GET /sources`), and dash proxies them at `/api/jobs/*` to back its whole **Jobs** page — listings always on screen, with Wanted, Suggestions, Radar, Documents and Applications panels around it, and six Playwright specs. ⚠️ dash's `/api/jobs/*` is job-store, **not** the scheduler; the scheduler's own `/api/jobs/` is reached at dash `/api/scheduler/jobs/*`. Driven by two enabled scheduler jobs: `job-radar-dispatch` (57, daily 08:30) and `job-tailor-dispatch` (58, `*/5`). Module `github.com/kayushkin/job-store`, root package `jobstore`, SQLite at `~/.config/job-store/job-store.db` (WAL, foreign keys on). `CONTRACT.md` is the route table. ⚠️ The repo has **no `origin` remote**, so nothing here has left this box. |
| **quote-store** | Service | Go | `:8309`. Quotes worth keeping, split into the three things a quote actually is: the passage (`quotes`), who said it (`authors`) and the book, talk or essay it came out of (`works`). A quote points at both by id, so renaming an author moves every quote of theirs instead of orphaning them. Passages dedupe on a signature — the text lowercased with punctuation and repeated whitespace removed — so the same passage pasted twice with different quote marks lands on one row. Search is an fts5 index over the passage, its tags and note, **and** the author and work names, kept true by triggers on every write path including a rename and a retitle. `DELETE` is reversible, `?hard=true` purges and frees the signature. `GET /quotes/random?format=text` renders the passage with its attribution for a digest or a shell prompt. Routes are rooted at `/`, and `CONTRACT.md` is the route table. dash proxies them at `/api/quotes/*` to back its **Quotes** page (top navbar → 📖 Quotes): the passages with the attribution the store joined, tag chips that double as the tag list and the filter, an author filter, a shuffle and a small composer, with eight Playwright specs in `dash/e2e/quotes.spec.ts`. Module `github.com/kayushkin/quote-store`, root package `quotestore`, SQLite at `~/.config/quote-store/quote-store.db` (WAL). Built with `-tags sqlite_fts5`, which is not optional: without it the binary starts and dies at the first write. ⚠️ Like job-store, the repo has **no `origin` remote**. |
