## LLM Bridge (Chat & Agent Harness System)

The llm-bridge ecosystem is the current default for chat and agent management. It replaced the older per-agent NATS adapters (claude-code-adapter, openclaw-adapter), which were decommissioned 2026-06-05 (local repos removed; GitHub repos archived).

### Core

| Project | Type | Language | Description |
|---------|------|----------|-------------|
| **llm-bridge** | Library | Go | Canonical message types (`msg/`) and bridge interfaces (`bridge/`). The lingua franca for the entire ecosystem — all harnesses and providers import this. |
| **llm-bridge-server** | Service | Go | Central HTTP gateway and session server. Manages harness lifecycle, SSE event streaming, credential bindings. Orchestrates agent-store, memory-store, harness-store, model-store. |
| **llm-bridge-adapter** | Service | Go | NATS bus adapter bridging llm-bridge-server with the inber messaging ecosystem. Translates between NATS pub/sub and HTTP/SSE. |
| **llm-bridge-runner** | Daemon | Go | Registers a remote machine with an llm-bridge-server and accepts harness-spawn requests over a single **outbound** WebSocket, so the server can drive harness subprocesses on machines behind NAT without inbound SSH or a VPN. |

